  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Vaugrenier beach is at the western end of Villeneuve-Loubet, on the Antibes side: a natural beach with a water-sports base on site and access via the cycle path.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The Villeneuve-Loubet tourist office states that it is the only beach in the town that accepts animals, and that it is open daily, closed from midnight to 6am. Barbecues are banned. The office doesn't detail the leash rule; a Cannes tourist office document (2023) says "animals kept on a leash", which remains the cautious choice. Access is free and the beach is open all year 2026. No official source mentions a dog shower or a specific type of ground.</p>
      <p><strong>Check before you go:</strong> the tourist office listing for La Batterie beach (west side of the Marina port) also carries the mention "Pets accepted", which contradicts the "only beach in the town" wording of the Vaugrenier listing. Ask the office (04 92 02 66 16) about the rule in force before settling anywhere other than Vaugrenier.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Vaugrenier departmental nature park, on the other side of the road, accepts dogs on a leash; the Department's rules require a collar and leash all year.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Vaugrenier departmental nature park (about a hundred hectares of woods, meadows and a pond, with free access) is open from 7am to 8pm from 1 April to 31 October and from 8am to 6pm from 1 November to 31 March, according to Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme. The listing says "animals accepted, on a leash". The park's rules ban animals from the developed areas (play areas, educational areas, fitness, sports courses) and first-category dogs; second-category dogs must be muzzled.</p>
      <p>As for beaches, the Villeneuve-Loubet tourist office also describes La Batterie beach (west side of the Marina port): natural-material beach, beach restaurants and shops nearby, showers, supervised beach and the mention "pets accepted". Hippodrome beach in Cagnes-sur-Mer, where the last quarter of the beach is open to dogs according to the Cannes tourist office, is a few minutes away by car.</p>
